- BUG:
    -if expecting expression but got eof will make the compiler get stuck
        even doing checks for eof seems to not work unless the file ended with a line feed
    - the compiler does not handle a case of returning a value in a void function.
        the compiler will interpret 'return expr' as a void return and as a separate expression.
        there is no way currently to detect this without the lexer automatically inserting semicolon tokens which it does not do.
    - a statement such as 'var my_slice: []i32 = [1, 2, 3]' will actually compile to an array instead of a slice.

design issues:
    - currently constness is basically immutability. but const keyword should be used entirely for compile time only.
        i can introduce a new keyword called imut to take consts job (THEYTOOKOURJOBSSS).
        i can also use the let keyword for top level immutable vars.
    - literals and type coercion need addressing.
        use a better way to coerce types such as in the analyzer check if the checked type and the context type dont match
        then try to do a coercion.
        literals should be coerced to whatever type is is most viable in its context.
        integer suffixes should also be added for greater ease of use.

warnings to add:
