- misc:
    - anonymous struct literals and types eg:

        var my_obj =
        {
            a: 10,
            s: "hello"
        }

        var my_obj: {a: i32, s: str}

    - currently type coercion is unreliable. perhaps implement type coercion inside the analyzer so when a node is visited
        it will check the context type and if it is not equal to its own type it will do a coercion.
    - undefined keyword that can be used when setting the initial value of a variable. this will make it not initialize to its default value.
        useful for very large values that do not need default initialization.
    - make pointers have index operators.
    - implement warning system.
    - implement command line interface.
    - implement arithmetic operations for nested arrays such as [4][4]f32.
    - currently a lot of types have wonky sizes. implement more accurate sizes.
    - pure functions with the pure attribute. perhaps even automatic pure detection.
    - change keyword attributes to not actually be real keywords so they can be used for symbols. possibly just use structs defined inside core package.
    - bitwise operators
    - expressions like ^(ptr + 1) = 10 do not compile. that might be a good thing actually. but look into it someday.
    - improve literal analysis. literals should be coerced into anytype if they fit.
    - correctly handle float min and max value properties. currently its the same as integers which is obviously wrong.
    - replace recursive descent with operator precedent parsing (pratt parsing)
    - break and continue to label. possibly goto? probably a bad idea anyway
    - automatic va_list creation when passing ... to another function
    - manual va_list support
    - theres too much repeated work between the ast parser and the analyzer. and sometimes even the code gen.
    - compile time for loops
    - make types be responsible for how they can be casted to other types
    - floor div with //
    - stringify operator
    - currently shadowing works fine. but this was unintended. in the future i might want to consider disallowing it.
    - integral literal suffixes
    - typeof operator
    - assert statement
    - integral literals in other bases such as hex or binary
    - improve api for compiler functions
    - real type that can accept any integral value and automatically does the correct code gen depending on its current value
    - vardiac arguments
    - function overloading
    - runtime type information through a Type type
    - typeid system
    - type is expression
    - for loop where clause
    - references
